                    briefing_text_r2:       `Pick the pathway — <strong>exclusive license</strong>, <strong>inventor spin-off</strong>, or <strong>joint development</strong> — and match it to context, not to the headline upside. A TRL-4 asset with a reluctant lead inventor and two colliding clocks is a different problem than a field-proven one. The spin-off has the biggest payoff on paper, but the VC's €1.2M is conditional on the inventor leaving academia — and she has never run a company. The bare license is fast clean cash but surrenders control to a possibly conflicted incumbent. Decide the model, handle the key-person risk, and define when value transfers to a partner.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Allocate the seed fund & pick the partner`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `The arithmetic forces leverage: €180k filing + €450k validation exceeds the €600k seed fund, so internal money alone cannot both protect <em>and</em> de-risk the asset. Allocate the seed fund, decide which jurisdictions to file in (focus beats filing everywhere "to be safe"), and sign the partner who co-funds the gap. The construction group's €400k JDA co-funds validation; the multinational's clean €250k cash comes with surrendered control; the VC's €1.2M only counts if the inventor leaves. Maximise <strong>external euros pulled per internal euro</strong> — your funder measures you on leverage ≥1.5×.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Commit, sequence & recover`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Present the integrated plan to the investment committee. Sequence the next 12 months around the <strong>irreversible Day-90 deadlines</strong> — file the patent in week 1, start validation immediately, gate partner payments to milestones — because loose sequencing loses the patent <em>and</em> the cash. Set exit KPIs (TRL at exit, time-to-market, value created, leverage ratio) and build one contingency for the things that can still break the plan: the inventor walking or the field validation slipping in month nine.`,

